From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] comdlg32: activate and show the file list's view

Purpose: show the file list of the explorer-style open and save dialogs
when the shell view is Windows' (in the Windows 7 shell session every
program has Windows 7's shell32).
Windows behavior: a shell browser activates the view it created
(IShellView::UIActivate) and shows its window; Windows' view window is
created hidden.
Wine before: comdlg32 relied on Wine's view, which shows itself; with
Windows 7's shell32 the dialog had an empty space where the list is.
Change: after CreateViewWindow, UIActivate(SVUIA_ACTIVATE_NOFOCUS) and
show the view window if it is hidden.
Evidence: Notepad's Open dialog lists the folder with Windows 7's
shell32 (its SHELLDLL_DefView and SysListView32 existed, hidden); with
Wine's shell32 the dialog is drawn as before.
Scope: comdlg32's explorer-style dialogs.
---
 dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
index 476bc20..b36f1e7 100644
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
@@ -415,6 +415,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IShellBrowserImpl_BrowseObject(IShellBrowser *iface,
 
     fodInfos->ShellInfos.hwndView = hwndView;
 
+    /* A browser activates and shows the view it created; Wine's view shows
+     * itself, Windows' (Windows 7's shell32) waits for the browser. */
+    IShellView_UIActivate(psvTmp, SVUIA_ACTIVATE_NOFOCUS);
+    if (!IsWindowVisible(hwndView)) ShowWindow(hwndView, SW_SHOWNA);
+
     /* Set view window control id to 5002 */
     SetWindowLongPtrW(hwndView, GWLP_ID, lst2);
     /* The view has already drawn its list in the list's own font, whose item
